    <h1>North Goa vs South Goa: start with the trip you want</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">Goa’s regions are not interchangeable hotel zones. Pick the part of the coast that fits your plans, then compare the individual property’s location and facilities.</p>

    <h2>North Goa: several different beach bases</h2>
    <p>The properties in this guide’s North Goa shortlist span Sinquerim-Candolim, Nerul, Vagator and Calangute. The Government of Goa groups these and Anjuna within a wider North Goa beach circuit. That range can suit a trip built around choosing among different coastal areas, but it does not make every hotel a convenient base for every beach.</p>
    <p>The hotel options also differ in scale: <a href="/hotels/taj-fort-aguada-goa/">Taj Fort Aguada</a> has direct Sinquerim Beach access, <a href="/hotels/ahilya-by-the-sea/">Ahilya by the Sea</a> is a nine-room, three-villa property in Nerul, <a href="/hotels/w-goa-vagator/">W Goa</a> is in Vagator, and <a href="/hotels/calangute-residency/">Calangute Residency</a> is the GTDC-listed option in Calangute.</p>

    <h2>South Goa: compare beach access property by property</h2>
    <p>The selected South Goa stays cover Arossim-Cansaulim, Majorda, Colva and Benaulim. They lean toward resort stays, but the way each reaches the coast differs: <a href="/hotels/itc-grand-goa/">ITC Grand Goa</a> has direct Arossim Beach access, <a href="/hotels/alila-diwa-goa/">Alila Diwa Goa</a> lists a shuttle to Gonsua Beach, <a href="/hotels/courtyard-by-marriott-goa-colva/">Courtyard Goa Colva</a> is described by Marriott as steps from Colva Beach, and <a href="/hotels/taj-exotica-goa/">Taj Exotica</a> is in beachfront Benaulim.</p>
    <p>This can fit a stay centred on the resort or nearby beach. The locations are still spread along the coast; check the address and transport for the activities you plan rather than treating South Goa as one walkable resort strip.</p>

